        dim (Union[int, str]): Dimension to be unflattened
        unflattened_size (Union[torch.Size, Tuple, List, NamedShape]): New shape of the unflattened dimension

    Examples:
        >>> input = torch.randn(2, 50)
        >>> # With tuple of ints
        >>> m = nn.Sequential(
        >>>     nn.Linear(50, 50),
        >>>     nn.Unflatten(1, (2, 5, 5))
        >>> )
        >>> output = m(input)
